        "width": 900,
        "height": 876,
        "content": "## Campaign Co-pilot — read every reply, tune the agent that writes them\n\nYour outbound campaign throws off signal every single day — which objections keep repeating, which step stopped earning replies, whether the reply rate is quietly sliding. Normally **nobody reads that in aggregate**, so campaigns drift and the fix lands weeks late. This workflow does that review for you every morning and turns it into **one Slack digest with one-click agent tuning**.\n\n### Why Twain\nTwain isn't mail-merge. Each campaign runs on an AI **Agent** that researches every lead and writes personalized outreach from a brief you set in plain language. Because the copy comes from an agent, it can be **improved**: Twain reads the campaign's real replies, tells you what's working and what isn't, and updates the Agent so the next messages reflect it. Research → personalized copy → **learn from the replies** — one closed loop, no analyst required.\n\n### What it does\n• Pulls each campaign's HeyReach stats + reply threads once a day\n• Twain analyzes reply themes, per-step performance, and health signals (reply-rate trend, connection acceptance, sequence exhaustion, stalls) — server-side, **free**\n• Posts a short Slack digest that leads with the biggest lever, and applies approved Agent changes with one click\n\n### Why it's helpful\n• The campaign review that never gets done, done every morning\n• **Credits are only spent when there's new signal** — health checks + the gate are free, quiet healthy days stay silent\n• You approve every change; nothing auto-sends, and every Agent edit is versioned + reversible\n\n### How to set up\n1. Create a Twain account + campaign at **https://www.twain.ai** — the campaign's Agent writes the outreach and is what gets tuned.\n2. Add each `{ twain_campaign_id, heyreach_campaign_id, focus }` to the **Settings** node.\n3. Wire the credentials: HeyReach (Header Auth), Twain (Header Auth, `X-Api-Key`), Slack.\n\nBuilt with Twain — https://www.twain.ai"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
